/*
 * Example 01 — Hello Passthrough
 * ================================
 * The simplest possible Sigil pipeline.
 *
 * CONCEPTS INTRODUCED:
 *   - broker    : connection to a message broker
 *   - pipeline  : a named data processing flow
 *   - source    : where messages come from
 *   - sink      : where messages go
 *
 * WHAT IT DOES:
 *   Subscribes to "sensors/temperature" and forwards every message
 *   unchanged to "mirror/temperature". A simple relay.
 *
 * GENERATED CODE:
 *   sigil generate examples/01_hello_passthrough.sigil -o out/
 *   Creates a Python app that subscribes and republishes messages.
 */

// Step 1: Define a broker — where your data lives.
// At minimum, you need a host and port.
broker local
    host: "localhost"
    port: 1883
end

// Step 2: Define a pipeline — what to do with the data.
// A pipeline needs at least a source and a sink.
pipeline relay
    // Subscribe to incoming messages
    source from local :: "sensors/temperature"

    // Republish them somewhere else (unchanged)
    |> sink to local :: "mirror/temperature"
end

